<title>USA: U.S. debt futures hold higher after two-year sale.</title>
<headline>U.S. debt futures hold higher after two-year sale.</headline>
<text>
<p>July 22 - U.S. debt futures stayed firm after the two-year sold for 5.930 pct high yield, 2.53 bid/cover, $1.04 billion non-comps. Market focused on Humphrey-Hawkins testimony. Sept T-bond cap seen at 114-15/32 to 17/32 and 114-22/32, the 6.50-pct yield equivalent.</p>
